        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "4f040469-c94b-365b-9637-9e7f2829b04f",
                "word": "improprement",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "69837f8d-4db6-3246-807b-ca8b0d5b359b",
                        "entry_id": "4f040469-c94b-365b-9637-9e7f2829b04f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "D’une manière impropre, en parlant du langage."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c368d0b5-53d8-4fdf-9d0d-b317c456d8a5",
                                "sense_id": "69837f8d-4db6-3246-807b-ca8b0d5b359b",
                                "text": "Beaucoup des tripolis et des randanites (ou Kieselguhr), dites souvent improprement « terres d'Infusoires », qui sont employées dans l'industrie, se sont ainsi formés autrefois dans les lacs de notre pays d'Auvergne, […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b82fdd80-2b3c-4e0c-b98d-c93d726f70db",
                                "sense_id": "69837f8d-4db6-3246-807b-ca8b0d5b359b",
                                "text": "C'est alors [par les casuistes] que l’on sut qu’on peut pour une pomme, Sans blesser la justice, assassiner un homme ; Assassiner ! ah ! non, je parle improprement […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "63c48d47-2dd1-46f4-baff-31f2679c5529",
                                "sense_id": "69837f8d-4db6-3246-807b-ca8b0d5b359b",
                                "text": "Jean Duns, écossais, nommé improprement Scot, et connu en son temps par le titre de docteur subtil."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0c2be055-e9d0-4ba7-b792-f4b1d1f5a723",
                        "source_entry_id": "4f040469-c94b-365b-9637-9e7f2829b04f",
                        "source_sense_id": "69837f8d-4db6-3246-807b-ca8b0d5b359b",
                        "target_lang_word": "improperly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "improperly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea0da7fe-9ff9-3922-a962-9f557d93b6ba",
                                        "entry_id": "7eaa251a-f65e-3f29-a735-76cd9be3ac32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In an improper manner; not properly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "096a272b-367c-46f7-adce-3558766ce7a6",
                                                "sense_id": "ea0da7fe-9ff9-3922-a962-9f557d93b6ba",
                                                "text": "Prosecutors also said Wednesday their side “does not intend to reference allegations that the defendant violated FARA or improperly coordinated with the Obama Administration,” referring to the Foreign Agents Registration Act, which requires people who lobby on behalf of foreign clients to register beforehand with the US government."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "71c030b6-803e-425e-a083-c1585e283e6d",
                        "source_entry_id": "4f040469-c94b-365b-9637-9e7f2829b04f",
                        "source_sense_id": "69837f8d-4db6-3246-807b-ca8b0d5b359b",
                        "target_lang_word": "incorrectly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "incorrectly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d4897038-4457-3b45-b0c7-34d67faf1ba7",
                                        "entry_id": "cd028e19-ec1b-319f-9954-537a070cd587",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In an incorrect manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eee1b6de-9971-42e4-8bde-2941305694be",
                                                "sense_id": "d4897038-4457-3b45-b0c7-34d67faf1ba7",
                                                "text": "I lost a few marks in the test for spelling words incorrectly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06b59dd3-8cb9-4674-b531-e5c2109c565b",
                                                "sense_id": "d4897038-4457-3b45-b0c7-34d67faf1ba7",
                                                "text": "In March 2008, the name was reapplied incorrectly as County of Durham, but this was also removed by February 2009."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f43597a-be16-4c69-aa4e-76724d8ef5f4",
                                                "sense_id": "d4897038-4457-3b45-b0c7-34d67faf1ba7",
                                                "text": "A RIF notice received by one FDA employee on Tuesday included performance ratings that were incorrectly low, meaning the severance pay offered was lower than it would be for the ratings they previously received, the employee told CNN."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ad82b866-741e-4b95-8e48-c25987e099a1",
                        "source_entry_id": "4f040469-c94b-365b-9637-9e7f2829b04f",
                        "source_sense_id": "69837f8d-4db6-3246-807b-ca8b0d5b359b",
                        "target_lang_word": "unfitly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "unfitly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab8398cf-0b8b-3fa5-a8f1-fda8b634447c",
                                        "entry_id": "53977e52-725e-340b-879c-d3035363ac37",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In an unfit manner; unsuitably, inappropriately, not fitly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1be7ef8f-33cc-4b5a-9962-89a73a29cfb6",
                                                "sense_id": "ab8398cf-0b8b-3fa5-a8f1-fda8b634447c",
                                                "text": "These two sorts of essences, I suppose, may not unfitly be termed, the one the REAL, the other NOMINAL ESSENCE. 16."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6838376e-c831-41b3-97ad-5fbb7b149abf",
                                                "sense_id": "ab8398cf-0b8b-3fa5-a8f1-fda8b634447c",
                                                "text": "And in reference to this harmonious interplay of all the human faculties and sensibilities, I may not unfitly apply to Shakespeare's workmanship these choice lines from Wordsworth: \"Brisk Youth appeared, the Morn of youth, With freaks of graceful folly,-- Life's temperate Noon, her sober Eve, Her Night not melancholy; Past, present, future, all appeared, In harmony united, Like guests that meet, and some from far, By cordial love invited.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7557e97-b6ad-4a22-8f29-3887b9ef85b4",
                                                "sense_id": "ab8398cf-0b8b-3fa5-a8f1-fda8b634447c",
                                                "text": "He had said he would, but had dawdled skillfully and was still unfitly in bare feet and the shabby garments of a weekday."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c1daa0b5-445f-4455-8518-272464dac40e",
                        "source_entry_id": "4f040469-c94b-365b-9637-9e7f2829b04f",
